BC-250: don't route VM/TLB flushes through KIQ

On the BC-250 (gfx1013 / cyan skillfish) the GRBM/CP register range
0x2000-0x2FFF reads back 0xFFFFFFFF -- those IP blocks are disabled on the
die. KIQ lives there, so any VM/TLB flush routed through it never completes:

    amdgpu: Timeout waiting for VM flush hub: 0!
    amdgpu: GPU mode1 reset ... VRAM is lost due to GPU reset!
    amdgpu: ring sdma1 test failed (-110)

This makes any ROCm/PyTorch workload die on its first device allocation.
Bare hipMalloc+hipMemcpy still works, so the flush path is only reached
under certain allocation patterns.

STATUS: candidate fix, NOT yet confirmed to resolve the PyTorch hang.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@
-	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = !amdgpu_emu_mode;
+	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = false; /* BC-250 fix: KIQ dead */
